content.text:
Here is a comprehensive summary of the fullscreen feature implementation in the codebase:

---

## Fullscreen Feature Implementation

The fullscreen feature is **entirely implemented within the HTML/JS that runs inside a WebView** for the exercise editor. There is no React Native-level fullscreen, no `ScreenOrientation`, `NavigationBar`, or `immersive` mode APIs used. The app uses the **HTML Fullscreen API** (standard browser API).

### 1. Core Fullscreen Implementation

**File:** `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/utils/editor/exerciseHtml.ts`

This file generates the complete HTML document displayed inside a `react-native-webview` for each exercise. The fullscreen functionality is built into this HTML page directly.

#### The Fullscreen Button (Maximize Button)

- **Lines 160-171 (CSS styles):** The `.maximize-btn` class styles a button in the preview section header.
- **Lines 416-418 (HTML):** A button with `id="maximize-btn"` labeled "Toggle fullscreen preview" is rendered in the "Your Output" preview section header:
  ```html
  <button class="maximize-btn" id="maximize-btn" title="Toggle fullscreen preview">
    <span id="maximize-icon" style="font-size:16px; color:${colors.onSurfaceVariant}">&#x26F6;</span>
  </button>
  ```

#### Fullscreen CSS

- **Lines 190-206:** Two CSS rules handle the fullscreen state using the `:fullscreen` and `-webkit-full-screen` pseudo-classes on the `.sketch-box` element:
  ```css
  .sketch-box:fullscreen {
    width: 100vw;
    height: 100vh;
    background: #000000;
    border-radius: 0;
  }
  ```
  These make the sketch box fill the entire viewport when in fullscreen mode. Canvas elements inside are constrained to `max-width: 100%` and `max-height: 100%`.

#### Fullscreen Toggle JavaScript

**Lines 1368-1411** contain the full JavaScript logic:

- **`maximizeBtn` click handler (lines 1373-1398):**
  ```javascript
  maximizeBtn.addEventListener('click', function() {
    var sketch = document.getElementById('user-sketch');
    var el = sketch;
    var fsElement = document.fullscreenElement || document.webkitFullscreenElement || document.webkitCurrentFullScreenElement;
    var isExpanded = !!fsElement || (sketch && sketch.classList.contains('expanded'));
    if (isExpanded) {
      // Exit fullscreen
      if (document.exitFullscreen) { document.exitFullscreen().catch(function(){}); }
      else if (document.webkitExitFullscreen) { document.webkitExitFullscreen(); }
      if (sketch) sketch.classList.remove('expanded');
      setMaximizeIcon(false);
    } else if (el) {
      // Enter fullscreen
      var req = el.requestFullscreen || el.webkitRequestFullscreen || el.webkitRequestFullScreen;
      if (req) {
        var p = req.call(el);
        if (p && p.catch) p.catch(function(){});
        el.classList.add('expanded');
      } else {
        // Fullscreen API unavailable — fall back to inline expanded box
        el.classList.add('expanded');
        setTimeout(function() { smoothScrollTo(el, 300); }, 350);
      }
      setMaximizeIcon(true);
    }
  });
  ```

  Key behavior:
  - Uses the **HTML Fullscreen API** (`element.requestFullscreen()` / `document.exitFullscreen()`) with vendor-prefixed fallbacks for WebKit (`webkitRequestFullscreen`, `webkitExitFullscreen`, `webkitFullscreenElement`).
  - If the Fullscreen API is unavailable (older WebView), it **falls back** to expanding the sketch box inline by toggling the `.expanded` CSS class, which transitions the height from `180px` to `400px`.
  - Toggles the icon between `&#x26F6;` (expand) and `&#x2715;` (close).

- **Icon synchronization (lines 1400-1411):** Listens for `fullscreenchange`, `webkitfullscreenchange`, and `webkitcurrentfullscreenchange` events on the `document` to keep the icon and `.expanded` class in sync when the user exits fullscreen via browser controls (e.g., pressing Escape):
  ```javascript
  function onFsChange() {
    var fsElement = document.fullscreenElement || document.webkitFullscreenElement || document.webkitCurrentFullScreenElement;
    var sketch = document.getElementById('user-sketch');
    if (sketch) {
      if (fsElement) { sketch.classList.add('expanded'); setMaximizeIcon(true); }
      else { sketch.classList.remove('expanded'); setMaximizeIcon(false); }
    }
  }
  document.addEventListener('fullscreenchange', onFsChange);
  document.addEventListener('webkitfullscreenchange', onFsChange);
  document.addEventListener('webkitcurrentfullscreenchange', onFsChange);
  ```

#### Inline Expanded State

- **Lines 172-186 (CSS):** The `.sketch-box` has a default height of `180px` with a CSS transition on height. When `.expanded` is added, height goes to `400px`:
  ```css
  .sketch-box { height: 180px; transition: height 0.3s ease; }
  .sketch-box.expanded { height: 400px; }
  ```

### 2. Status Bar

**File:** `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/components/StatusBarAccent.tsx` (32 lines)

This component renders a `<StatusBar>` from `expo-status-bar` that:
- Reads the `setting_showStatusBar` setting from `AsyncStorage` on mount.
- If the setting is `"false"`, renders a **hidden** status bar (`<StatusBar style="hidden" hidden />`).
- Otherwise, renders the status bar with a style (`"dark"` or `"light"`) determined by the luminance of the accent color, and a `backgroundColor` matching the theme.

**File:** `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/_layout.tsx` (line 42)

The `StatusBarAccent` component is rendered in the root layout:
```tsx
<StatusBarAccent />
```

**File:** `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/settings/index.tsx` (lines 321-334)

The Settings screen has a **"Status Bar" toggle** switch (lines 321-334) that allows users to show/hide the status bar. This setting is persisted to `AsyncStorage` under `setting_showStatusBar` and is loaded by `StatusBarAccent` on app startup.

### 3. App Orientation

**File:** `/workspaces/learn-p5/app.json` (line 6)

The app's orientation is set to `"portrait"` at the Expo config level:
```json
"orientation": "portrait"
```

### 4. What is NOT present

- No `ScreenOrientation` / `expo-screen-orientation` package or API calls.
- No `NavigationBar` or `navigationBar` related code (Android system navigation bar hiding).
- No `immersive` mode configuration.
- No dedicated React Native fullscreen components or native module usage.
- The fullscreen is purely web-based within the exercise editor's WebView.

### Summary of Relevant Files

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/utils/editor/exerciseHtml.ts` | **Primary fullscreen implementation** — HTML/CSS/JS that provides the fullscreen toggle for the p5.js sketch preview within the WebView (lines 160-206 for CSS, 416-418 for HTML button, 1368-1411 for JS logic) |
| `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/components/StatusBarAccent.tsx` | Status bar visibility and styling component (32 lines) |
| `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/_layout.tsx` | Root layout that renders `StatusBarAccent` (line 42) |
| `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/settings/index.tsx` | Settings screen with "Status Bar" toggle (lines 321-334) |
| `/workspaces/learn-p5/src/app/learn/[course]/[id].tsx` | Exercise screen that hosts the WebView rendering the fullscreen-enabled HTML |
| `/workspaces/learn-p5/app.json` | Expo config with `"orientation": "portrait"` (line 6) |
